<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beira</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beira is a port city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>, at the mouth of the Pungwe River on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. Founded in 1887, it became the capital of the Mozambique Company and the terminus of a railway that reached the British colonies inland by 1899. It has since served as a main outlet for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a> and is Mozambique's second port.</p></div>
